{"id":"steinbeck-charley-1960","title":"Steinbeck: Travels with Charley","who":"John Steinbeck and Charley the poodle","when":"September–December 1960","vehicle":"GMC pickup camper \"Rocinante\"","kind":"car","color":"#9a3412","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"Travels with Charley: In Search of America","by":"John Steinbeck"},{"kind":"book","title":"Dogging Steinbeck","by":"Bill Steigerwald","note":"Fact-checks the trip"}],"summary":"At 58, Steinbeck sets out to rediscover the country he writes about: almost 10,000 miles round the edge of the United States in a camper named after Don Quixote's horse, with his wife's poodle. Maine potato fields, the Great Lakes, Montana which he loved, the Pacific Northwest, a farewell to his Salinas Valley, a Texas Thanksgiving and the ugly school protests of New Orleans. Later research showed he was rarely alone and tidied up the story.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Travels with Charley","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Travels_with_Charley"},{"label":"Bill Steigerwald, \"Sorry, Charley\" (Reason, 2011)","url":"http://reason.com/archives/2011/04/04/sorry-charley"}],"approximate":"Places named in the book; the roads are approximate.","km":13827,"bbox":[-123.3938,29.9555,-67.8396,47.8133],"stops":[{"name":"Sag Harbor","place":"Sag Harbor, New York","at":[40.9979,-72.2922],"date":"Sept 1960","text":"Delayed two weeks by Hurricane Donna, he leaves his Long Island summer home.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Monumento_a_Cervantes_%28Madrid%29_10f.jpg/500px-Monumento_a_Cervantes_%28Madrid%29_10f.jpg","page":"Rocinante","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monumento_a_Cervantes_%28Madrid%29_10f.jpg","credit":"Manuel Martín Vicente from Spain","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Bangor","place":"Bangor, Maine","at":[44.8016,-68.7713],"text":"North through New England, closed summer shops and terse farmers.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Bangor%2C_Maine.jpg/500px-Bangor%2C_Maine.jpg","page":"Bangor, Maine","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bangor%2C_Maine.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Deer Isle","place":"Deer Isle, Maine","at":[44.224,-68.6776],"text":"The best lobster he ever ate, and a cat named George.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Mill_Creek_and_Town_Hall%2C_Deer_Isle%2C_ME.jpg/500px-Mill_Creek_and_Town_Hall%2C_Deer_Isle%2C_ME.jpg","page":"Deer Isle, Maine","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mill_Creek_and_Town_Hall%2C_Deer_Isle%2C_ME.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Northern Maine","place":"Presque Isle, Maine","at":[46.6812,-68.0155],"text":"A night with French-Canadian potato pickers, sharing wine.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Presque_Isle%2C_Maine.jpg/500px-Presque_Isle%2C_Maine.jpg","page":"Presque Isle, Maine","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Presque_Isle%2C_Maine.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Niagara Falls","place":"Niagara Falls, New York","at":[43.0848,-79.0702],"text":"Turned back at the Canadian border: Charley lacks his papers.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Niagara_Falls_001.JPG/500px-Niagara_Falls_001.JPG","page":"Niagara Falls, New York","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niagara_Falls_001.JPG","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Chicago","place":"Chicago, Illinois","at":[41.8756,-87.6244],"text":"A break with his wife Elaine in a hotel.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg/500px-Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg","page":"Chicago","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Sauk Centre","place":"Sauk Centre, Minnesota","at":[45.7377,-94.9524],"text":"Sinclair Lewis's home town, where nobody remembers him.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Original_Main_Street_HD.jpg/500px-Original_Main_Street_HD.jpg","page":"Sauk Centre, Minnesota","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Original_Main_Street_HD.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"North Dakota","place":"Fargo, North Dakota","at":[46.8772,-96.7898],"text":"Across the plains.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Downtown_Fargo_Aerial_-_Facing_Southeast_%2851009704407%29.jpg/500px-Downtown_Fargo_Aerial_-_Facing_Southeast_%2851009704407%29.jpg","page":"Fargo, North Dakota","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Fargo_Aerial_-_Facing_Southeast_%2851009704407%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Montana","place":"Missoula, Montana","at":[46.8701,-113.9953],"text":"The state he fell for, and the Great Divide.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg/500px-Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg","page":"Missoula, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Seattle","place":"Seattle, Washington","at":[47.6038,-122.3301],"text":"\"I wonder why progress looks so much like destruction.\"","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg/500px-Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg","page":"Seattle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Monterey","place":"Pacific Grove, California","at":[36.6211,-121.9178],"text":"Down the coast through Oregon (a flat tyre in the rain), to his old country. Farewell from Fremont Peak.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Pacific_Grove%2C_California_-_2022_5.jpg/500px-Pacific_Grove%2C_California_-_2022_5.jpg","page":"Pacific Grove, California","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pacific_Grove%2C_California_-_2022_5.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Mojave","place":"Barstow, California","at":[34.8986,-117.0244],"text":"Dog food for two coyotes instead of a bullet.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/City_View_of_Barstow%2C_California_from_Barstow_Road_%282013-12-08%29.jpg/500px-City_View_of_Barstow%2C_California_from_Barstow_Road_%282013-12-08%29.jpg","page":"Barstow, California","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:City_View_of_Barstow%2C_California_from_Barstow_Road_%282013-12-08%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Amarillo","place":"Amarillo, Texas","at":[35.2073,-101.8371],"text":"Thanksgiving on a cattle ranch.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Amarillo_Texas_Downtown.jpg/500px-Amarillo_Texas_Downtown.jpg","page":"Amarillo, Texas","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amarillo_Texas_Downtown.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"New Orleans","place":"New Orleans, Louisiana","at":[29.9575,-90.0629],"text":"The mothers screaming at a newly integrated school depress him deeply.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/New_Orleans_from_the_Air_September_2019_-_Central_Business_District_Skyline_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-New_Orleans_from_the_Air_September_2019_-_Central_Business_District_Skyline_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"New Orleans","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Orleans_from_the_Air_September_2019_-_Central_Business_District_Skyline_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"New York","place":"New York City","at":[4